.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt FSD-UFS 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsd-ufs
.Nd RavenBSD UFS filesystem server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq ufs:
scheme, opens one GPT partition from a
.Dq block:
device, mounts it through the
.Dq ufs-core
library, and serves the tree with the
.Dq file:
protocol that
.Xr vfsd 8
mounts.
The mount is read-write by default; setting
.Ev FSD_UFS_READ_ONLY
keeps it read-only.
.Pp
The server selects partition 1 by default.  The partition is read with the
24-byte
.Dq block:
protocol; the
.Sy LIST
reply supplies its first sector and length, so the UFS mount sees only the
partition and never the GPT headers.
A missing or corrupt UFS image is a startup error and the server exits
non-zero; it never serves a partially mounted tree.
.Sh MOUNT PROTOCOL
.Nm
opens
.Pa block:0 ,
reads
.Sy INFO
and
.Sy LIST
from it, and mounts the selected partition.
It then registers the
.Dq ufs:
scheme.
A client such as
.Xr vfsd 8
mounts it with the
.Dq file:
control operation
.Sy MOUNT :
.Dl mount /ufs ufs:
After that, opening
.Pa /ufs/path
routes
.Pa path
to
.Nm .
.Pp
The server root is the filesystem root; an empty path and
.Pa /
both name it.
Paths received from
.Xr vfsd 8
have no leading slash and are treated as mount-relative.
.Pp
Symbolic links are followed with a bound of 8 links per path.
A final symbolic link is not followed for
.Sy READLINK ,
so the target is returned instead of being resolved.
.Pp
Directory reads are sequential.  The server keeps the directory cursor in the
open-file description; a client that sends a nonzero wire offset gets
.Er EINVAL .
A buffer smaller than the next packed entry also returns
.Er EINVAL .
The open-file budget is 256 descriptions.
.Pp
Open with create, truncate or append, and the
.Sy MKDIR ,
.Sy UNLINK ,
.Sy RMDIR ,
.Sy RENAME ,
.Sy SYMLINK ,
.Sy CHMOD and
.Sy TRUNCATE
control operations are forwarded to
.Dq ufs-core .
Writes use the open-file cursor; a successful
.Sy SYNC
returns only after the inode table, cylinder groups, summaries, superblock and
block device have been flushed.
If the superblock records WAPBL, metadata changes are staged through the
journal before commit; an image without a journal uses the synchronous
inode/cylinder-group/superblock ordering.
.Pp
After an I/O error the server enters a read-only state and rejects later
mutations with
.Er EROFS ;
it never reports a failed write as durable.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FSD_UFS_PARTITION -compact
.It Ev FSD_UFS_DEVICE
Device path opened as a client, default
.Pa block:0 .
.It Ev FSD_UFS_PARTITION
One-based GPT partition index, default 1.  Zero mounts the whole device.
.It Ev FSD_UFS_SCHEME
Registered scheme name, default
.Dq ufs .
.It Ev FSD_UFS_READ_ONLY
One, true or yes for a read-only mount; zero, false or no for read-write.
The default is read-write.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/fsd-ufs.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
A missing path returns
.Er ENOENT ;
a component that is not a directory returns
.Er ENOTDIR ;
a path longer than 255 bytes or a symlink loop returns
.Er ENAMETOOLONG
or
.Er ELOOP .
A corrupt filesystem or block I/O failure returns
.Er EIO .
A mutation on a read-only mount, or after an I/O error, returns
.Er EROFS .
A full filesystem returns
.Er ENOSPC .
A protocol framing error returns
.Er EPROTO .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr blockd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr initfsd 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
